n\n3,963 880 109MB\n\nEnglish Pages 640 [322] Year 2015\n\nReport DMCA / Copyright\n\nDOWNLOAD FILE\n\n  * Author / Uploaded\n  * Bill Addis\n\nTable of contents :\nIntroduction\nChapter 1. Building and engineering in ancient times: 1000 B.C.-A.D. 500\nChapter 2. The medieval era: 500-1400\nChapter 3. The Renaissance: 1400-1630\nChapter 4. Global trading and the Age of Reason and Enlightenment: 1630-1750\nChapter 5. Engineering becomes a profession: 1750-1800\nChapter 6. The harmony of theory and practice: 1800-1860\nChapter 7. The birth of the modern building: 1860-1920\nChapter 8. Architectural engineering: 1920-1960\nChapter 9. The computer age and the greening of construction: 1960-present\nAfterword\nGlossary\nAppendix 1 \"Aims and Means,\" by Ove Arup\nAppendix 2 Iron and its Alloys\nAppendix 3 Concrete and Reinforced Concrete\nEndnotes\nBibliography\nFurther reading\nIndex--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBuilding: 3,000 Years of Design, Engineering and Construction - Bill Addis - Google Books (https://books.google.com/books/about/Building_3_000_Years_of_Design_Engineeri.html?id=s0NSuQEACAAJ)\nciteturn125search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: 19.6 years ago; Crawled: last month; \nEach chapter concentrates on the famous characters and unsung heroes of engineering history.\" \"Accompanying the narrative text are more than 750 color and black-and-white photographs, archival plans and drawings, and original technical diagrams, many from rare and specialized sources around the world. Sidebars highlight key developments, including the slide rule, the evolution of the structural frame, and the glass facade; major texts such as De Architecture by Vitruvius, and brief histories of key concepts such as calculus. Also included in the book are extensive reference materials: timelines, appendices, a glossary, notes, bibliography, and a guide to further reading.\"--BOOK JACKET.\n\n### About the author (2007)\n\nWilliam Addis is a consulting engineer at Buro Happold in London and the author of numerous books, academic papers, and book reviews on construction history published over the past 25 years. He holds a doctorate degree in the history and philosophy of engineering from the University of Reading, where he taught this subject for 15 years; he has also delivered lecture courses on engineering history at Cambridge University, the University of Bath, and University College, London. In 1998, he helped curate the exhibition \"The Art of the Engineer\" at the Pompidou Centre in Paris and contributed to the book that accompanied the exhibition. Addis is an active member of the Institution of Structural Engineers' History Study Group and lectures at professional conferences around the world.\n\n### Bibliographic information\n\nTitle  | Building: 3,000 Years of Design, Engineering and Construction\nAuthor  | Bill Addis\nEdition  | illustrated, reprint\nPublisher  | Phaidon Press, 2007\nISBN  | 0714841463, 9780714841465\nLength  | 608 pages\nSubjects  | Architecture › History › General\nArchitecture / History / General--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBuilding: 3,000 years of design engineering and construction. | ALA (https://www.ala.org/winner/building-3000-years-design-engineering-and-construction)\nciteturn125search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; \n\n# Building: 3,000 years of design engineering and construction.\n\nAddis, Bill; Phaidon, 2007\n\n## About\n\n## Details\n\nISBN:\n\n9780714841465\n\n## Awards Won\n\n | Title  | Year\n--- | --- | ---\n | PPO Test  | 2010 - Selection(s)--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSELECTED BIBLIOGRAPHY. (https://www.constructionhistory.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2014/09/CHS-Bibliography.pdf)\nciteturn125search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8 months ago; \nSELECTED BIBLIOGRAPHY.  \nThe following guide to books on the history of construction and building 